  "summary": "Import-time directory listing exfiltrated to anonymous tunnel host",
  "details": "MRCL2/__init__.py imports core.py, which on module load calls os.listdir('.') and opens a raw TCP socket to hcagg-13-205-45-209.run.pinggy-free.link:41719 (pinggy-free.link is an anonymous TCP tunneling service), sending the current working directory's file listing. The payload is prefixed with a 'REMOVE CONNECTION CONNECTED' banner that disguises the beacon as noise. The package advertises itself as a 'document integrity utility', with no documented purpose that would require an outbound network beacon on import. Any environment that imports MRCL2 silently discloses its working-directory contents to an attacker-controlled tunnel endpoint.",
